/android/app/release

# Secrets. No *app* secret belongs in an .env — the Supabase publishable key is
# a compile-time default in lib/services/supabase.dart and every real secret
# lives in Supabase Function secrets. What .env is for is the developer tooling
# in tool/, which runs on a laptop and never ships: today that is GEMINI_API_KEY
# for tool/icon_gen. .env.example is committed as the template and is the only
# .env* file that may be; the negation must stay below the patterns it undoes.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!ios/Flutter/ephemeral/flutter_native_integration.env
!macos/Flutter/ephemeral/flutter_native_integration.env

# Supabase CLI scratch: linked-project ref, pooler URL, server versions. No
# credentials today, but it is machine-local state either way.
supabase/.temp/

# The old React web app, cloned in for reference only. It carries its own git
# repo, is not part of this Flutter project, and gets deleted once the rebuild
# is done — see CLAUDE.md.
Aporah-Family-Hub/

# Generated grocery icons, pending review. Never committed — they are copied
# into assets/grocery/ by tool/icon_gen/install.dart once they pass a look.
tool/icon_gen/out/
tool/icon_gen/catalog_lines.txt
tool/icon_gen/review/

tool/icon_gen/reframe_preview/
tool/icon_gen/merchant_preview/
